Generally speaking, whenever you have a `Dispose` or `DisposeAsync` method which might throw an exception, you can use a pattern similar to below to swallow any inner exception and to let the outer exception propagate cleanly.

```cs
ExceptionDispatchInfo? edi = null;
try
{
    DoMainWork();
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    edi = ExceptionDispatchInfo.Capture(ex);
}
finally
{
    try
    {
        DoDispose();
    }
    finally
    {
        edi?.Throw();
    }
}
```
